{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (-0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The central hole is called out with a tight H7 fit tolerance on page 1, but the title block specifies an I.Z.B.P. plating finish whose thickness will reduce the bore diameter and interfere with the mating shaft. The designer must either increase the minimum hole size to allow for the plating thickness or add a note masking the bore during plating."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Increase the lower limit of D12 by the maximum plating thickness, or add a note specifying that the ⌀16 H7 bore is to be masked during I.Z.B.P. plating."}]}
